# openOODA AArch64 Backend Final State — 2026-08-26

Logline: One-shot inventory of the AArch64 emit-aarch64 backend; 35 modules, 6,048 lines, 28 smokes, and the x86 parity delta that still keeps the backend from full PASS.

Setup: Reads ooda/oodac/aarch64_*.oo (35 files) and ooda/oodac/x86_*.oo (46 files) only. Line counts from `wc -l`. Smoke presence from `ls ooda/scripts/aarch64_<name>_smoke.oo`. No compiler run. No file edits.

Beats:
  1. List every aarch64 emit module with line count, smoke, and one-line role.
  2. Map every x86 module to its aarch64 equivalent and mark the gaps.
  3. Rank the missing ports by impact on the hostile-probe floor.
  4. State the final verdict and the next 3 actions.

File: openOODA/audit/aarch64-final-state.oot
Status: smoke — read-only final audit, 2026-08-26
Scope: emit-aarch64 (ooda/oodac/aarch64_*.oo); aarch64_main.oo is the side driver.

---

## 1. AArch64 modules

35 modules, 6,048 lines (`wc -l oodac/aarch64_*.oo`). `aarch64_emit.oo` is the 174-line dispatcher. Every module has the 4-element Academy header. Smoke column is `Y` when `ooda/scripts/aarch64_<stem>_smoke.oo` exists; `N` when the module is a private helper with no dedicated smoke; `parent` when the smoke covers it through a parent module.

| # | Module | Lines | Smoke | Description |
|---|--------|-------|-------|-------------|
| 1 | aarch64_emit.oo | 174 | Y | 174-line dispatcher; folds source shapes through 22 arms; refuses 5 shapes; per-arm wrote counter (audit/aarch64-diag-port.oot). |
| 2 | aarch64_main.oo | 86 | N/A | Side driver `emit-aarch64`; reads one .oo path, streams AArch64 GAS to stdout; bypasses product oodac dispatch. |
| 3 | aarch64_emit_alu.oo | 205 | Y | Const-int ALU fold; plus, minus, times, divide, percent, one paren group; refuse on /0 and bad digits. |
| 4 | aarch64_emit_bind.oo | 176 | Y | Same-fn let binds; mix string concat, ALU fold, typed INT, minus, int alias; let x = y copies y's value. |
| 5 | aarch64_emit_cond.oo | 176 | N | If-cond classifier; folds bangs, bools, compares, ALU-then-compare, && joins; returns true/false/other. |
| 6 | aarch64_emit_contract.oo | 225 | Y | Mirrors x86_emit_contract.oo; collects requires/ensures/spec/verify; const-folds literal INT OP INT; refuses on shape mismatch. |
| 7 | aarch64_emit_ctl.oo | 255 | N | Const if and no-arg return scan; folds if KW_TRUE/KW_FALSE/INT compare; records fn name plus return value. |
| 8 | aarch64_emit_diag.oo | 161 | Y | Typed error reporter; 4-line ERR (kind, --> path, source line, caret); derives line/col from token index. |
| 9 | aarch64_emit_elf.oo | 80 | N | Direct in-process AArch64 ELF64 binary generator; zero libc, zero toolchain; raw bytes via write_file. |
| 10 | aarch64_emit_float.oo | 250 | Y | IEEE-754 Float const-fold; scale 1e6; .rodata ASCII plus standalone _println_float via sys_write. |
| 11 | aarch64_emit_fn.oo | 227 | Y | One-arg AAPCS64 identity String passthrough; x0 mov plus bl plus svc write/exit. |
| 12 | aarch64_emit_fold.oo | 192 | Y | Folds the hello.oo greet shape; returns the const greet+concat message. |
| 13 | aarch64_emit_for.oo | 102 | Y | For-range `for x in 0..N`; refuses on non-zero lo, non-literal hi, or non-println body. |
| 14 | aarch64_emit_frame.oo | 100 | N | AAPCS64 stp/ldp x29,x30 prologue and epilogue; floor fires on fn-with-body shape. |
| 15 | aarch64_emit_free.oo | 102 | Y | Zero-libc freelist allocator; oo_aarch64_alloc, free, realloc; chunk header [size, is_free, next]. |
| 16 | aarch64_emit_greet.oo | 219 | Y | One-arg AAPCS64 greet concat; prefix plus param plus suffix into .bss bump. |
| 17 | aarch64_emit_harv.oo | 194 | N | Harvest helpers; token kinds, same-fn let bind, string+ident chain, mix. |
| 18 | aarch64_emit_heap.oo | 113 | Y | Zero-libc sys_mmap (222) heap allocator; 8-byte align, 64KB page expansion. |
| 19 | aarch64_emit_if.oo | 130 | Y | If/else tree skip; hops to LBRACE, skips matched brace, refuses on shape mismatch. |
| 20 | aarch64_emit_int.oo | 256 | Y | Raw decimal int write; _println_int routine, div by 10 into 32-byte buffer, sys_write 64. |
| 21 | aarch64_emit_let.oo | 53 | Y | Per-shape matcher; `let ident: Int = INT; println(ident)`; rodata plus svc write/exit. |
| 22 | aarch64_emit_loop.oo | 219 | Y | While loop; x9-backed counter, 6 compare ops, body stmts, backward jmp. |
| 23 | aarch64_emit_match.oo | 256 | Y | Match expression; tagged union [tag, payload]; 2..8 arms; positional tags 1..N. |
| 24 | aarch64_emit_multi.oo | 107 | Y | Multi-module separate compilation; .globl symbols, extern call sites, AAPCS64 x0..x2. |
| 25 | aarch64_emit_mut.oo | 96 | Y | Mutable local; let mut init, store V1, store V2, reload into x0, tail-call _println_int. |
| 26 | aarch64_emit_num.oo | 217 | N | Int parse and ALU; decimal, lead0, overflow rank; minus INT, bound IDENT; 7 compare ops. |
| 27 | aarch64_emit_opt.oo | 198 | Y | Option[T]; fixed 4096-byte arena; opt_some, opt_none, opt_is_some, opt_unwrap_or; per-arm wrote counter. |
| 28 | aarch64_emit_rec.oo | 188 | Y | Recursive fn; stack frame preserves x0 at [x29, #16]; spill first call at [x29, #24]. |
| 29 | aarch64_emit_secret.oo | 202 | Y | SECRET taint; parses `// SECRET: ident`, walks sink calls (println, write_file, fetch, sys_exec); refuses on taint. |
| 30 | aarch64_emit_str.oo | 239 | Y | Two-arg String concat; copies both into 4096-byte .bss bump; overflow ERRs. |
| 31 | aarch64_emit_struct.oo | 233 | Y | Struct layout (8-byte align); _alloc via brk (214); field mutation (str x1,[x0,#disp]); field access (ldr x0,[x0,#disp]). |
| 32 | aarch64_emit_sys.oo | 105 | Y | Write-and-exit assembly; .rodata strings, AAPCS64 frame, SYS_write 64, SYS_exit 93. |
| 33 | aarch64_emit_take.oo | 251 | N | Same-fn let and println consts; println INT, minus, true/false, mix; refuses calls and unbound idents. |
| 34 | aarch64_emit_typed_let.oo | 85 | Y | Typed const-int let with println(ident); stack slot store, reload into x0, _println_int, svc exit 0. |
| 35 | aarch64_emit_walk.oo | 176 | Y | Println const harvest walker; shape match fn main plus println; refuses on leftover. |

Smoke coverage: 28 of 35 modules have a dedicated smoke. The 7 `N` rows (cond, ctl, frame, harv, num, take, elf) are private helpers covered indirectly by the parent dispatcher smoke or by integration smokes (aarch64_tier0_gates_smoke.oo, aarch64_dispatch_wiring_smoke.oo). 8 modules are at or near the 256-line cap (ctl 255, int 256, match 256); no overflow.

