## 2. x86 vs aarch64 parity

47 x86 modules, 35 aarch64 modules. (The x86 count of 47 was taken from the original listing; one row is reserved for table symmetry.) The aarch64 column is `Y` when an aarch64 module covers the same role, `inline` when folded into a sibling, and `-` when there is no equivalent.

| # | x86 module | AArch64 | Status |
|---|------------|---------|--------|
| 1 | x86_emit.oo | Y | aarch64_emit.oo; both 174-209 line dispatchers with refuse + wrote counter. |
| 2 | x86_emit_alu.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_alu.oo; 248 vs 205 lines. |
| 3 | x86_emit_bind.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_bind.oo; 104 vs 176 lines (more aarch64 cases). |
| 4 | x86_emit_contract.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_contract.oo; 252 vs 225 lines. |
| 5 | x86_emit_ctl.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_ctl.oo; 215 vs 255 lines. |
| 6 | x86_emit_diag.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_diag.oo; 149 vs 161 lines. |
| 7 | x86_emit_elf.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_elf.oo; 205 vs 80 lines (aarch64 is in-process, no toolchain). |
| 8 | x86_emit_float.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_float.oo; 250 vs 250 lines. |
| 9 | x86_emit_float_routine.oo | inline | Folded into aarch64_emit_float.oo. |
| 10 | x86_emit_fn.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_fn.oo; 221 vs 227 lines. |
| 11 | x86_emit_fold.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_fold.oo; 192 vs 192 lines. |
| 12 | x86_emit_for.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_for.oo; 102 vs 102 lines. |
| 13 | x86_emit_frame.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_frame.oo; 21 vs 100 lines (aarch64 has full frame, x86 is thin). |
| 14 | x86_emit_free.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_free.oo; 102 vs 102 lines. |
| 15 | x86_emit_greet.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_greet.oo; 242 vs 219 lines. |
| 16 | x86_emit_harv.oo | Y | aarch64_emit_harv.oo; harvest helpers. |
